   "l": "What is brittle is easy to break apart;\nwhat is minute is easy to scatter.",
   "v": true,
   "n": "泮 is a borrowed graph: the character on the page is the one for river ice thawing and going to pieces in spring, and the word behind it is 判 'to split'. Other received editions simply print 判. Both are read pàn, so nothing changes in the mouth — only on the page.\n\nSome keep 泮 in its own sense and translate 'melts away', which suits brittle ice rather well. We follow the standard reading and leave the other here."
