   "l": "order it while it is not yet in disorder.",
   "v": true,
   "n": "治 and 亂 are the standing pair of Chinese political vocabulary — good order and its collapse — and a ruler's whole record was told in those two words. Here they are used of anything at all, not just a state.\n\n之 in both lines is the object pronoun 'it', with no antecedent stated. The thing is not named because the claim is meant to hold of everything."
