   "l": "so as to assist the ten-thousand things' being-so-of-themselves,\nand yet dares not act.",
   "v": true,
   "i": "and so helps the ten thousand things to be as they are of themselves, and never dares to act.",
   "n": "輔 is the whole politics of the book in one character. It is a cart word: the boards lashed along the sides of a wagon to keep the load from spilling. They hold it in; they do not pull it, and they do not choose the road.\n\nThe chapter's last word is 為, which is also the word it began working on at 為之於未有 — act on it before it is there — and the final line takes it back. Not 'never act', but 不敢, does not dare to: the restraint is a kind of respect, not a rule."
